From aad6823eeac7b9ffdbf2be172f2b8a516c2cb2d0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mark-vis <118430440+mark-vis@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 10:49:21 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 24/28] (b) v2, part b-3: \caption* label: a rule for the
 paragraph, not a list

Round-4 finding R4-L1 (R4V-F1): the label of \caption* started the
paragraph only before an explicit list of tokens (\\, \newline,
\vadjust, \@), so other primitives after the label acted in vertical
mode: in a \vbox, #1\unskip: #2 removed \abovecaptionskip (16.94pt ->
6.94pt), #1\kern3pt #2 gave a vertical kern, #1\hbox{ -- }#2 a box on
its own line. No \@makecaption of TeX Live has these after #1.

Now there is a rule: the paragraph is started before the primitives
whose meaning depends on the mode (\kern, \penalty, \hbox, \box, \copy,
\raise, \lower, \vadjust) and before \\, \newline and \@; not before
\par, \vskip, a space or a macro. The ones that print something warn,
as other material after the label does (\penalty, \vadjust and \@ do
not). \unskip, \unkern and \unpenalty directly after the label are
removed: they are meant for the end of the label, which is empty.

Test: caption-interface-001 TEST 30, four shapes in vertical mode
(\unskip with a colon, \kern, \hbox, \penalty); on the old code the
first three give other heights and the last one warns.
